## How the friend uses this template

1. **Define your style.** (Terse / verbose / detailed / etc.)
2. **Set your chat budget.** (Default: 200 words/msg, 3000 tokens/session.)
3. **Pick which roles you play.** (All 5 by default; deselect the ones you delegate.)
4. **Fill in the per-agent matrix.** (Which agent gets which roles from you.)
5. **Set the operator-action cadence.** (How often each agent should ask.)
6. **Document the response format.** (Approve / reject / modify / defer.)
7. **Set the escalation SLA.** (Per-priority response time.)
8. **Document the feedback format.** (You're doing X. The right behavior is Y. Reason: Z.)
9. **Document the curator cycle.** (When do you write skills / SOULs / templates?)
10. **Document the fallback pattern.** (What do you do when the agent fails?)
11. **Schedule the quarterly audit.** (Use the 5-question audit.)

The operator interaction patterns are **operator-context.** The friend running Alice's methodology designs their own patterns for their own context. They do NOT copy the operator's specific patterns; they apply the method to derive their own.